WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.730
You become friends with girls
before you realize, Kei.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.530
It'd be good for you to make
some more friends, too.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.630
Do you mean male friends?

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:16.450
It doesn't matter what gender,
but it'd be more fun to see you talking to girls.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.540
Who do you recommend in that regard?

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.640
Nonoh, maybe?

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.580
I'll do what I can.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.890
That's what happened.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.860
I see.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.340
I understand your situation.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.720
So, could you be friends with me?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.340
Let's see...

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.460
If you bring me some cream puffs from
Sangatsudou next time you come here.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.550
I will.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.230
Thank you.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.670
<i>I achieved my goal very quickly.</i>

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:56.660
<i>I had a feeling making friends would
be a more time-consuming activity.</i>

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.400
<i>I'd never guess it was so simple.</i>

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.960
For now, sit here.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.710
I will.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.920
A Day in the Life of Haruki

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.380
Actually...

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.460
Yes?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.260
What do you think being friends means?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.760
I've researched that topic a lot.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.980
Friends seem to study together, have fun,
text, and talk on the phone at length.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.560
Texts and long phone calls?

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.150
I don't know your number.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.770
What should we do, then?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.690
Let me think...

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.820
Okay, put your number in my phone.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.660
Haruki... Misora.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.960
So your given name is Misora.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.420
Yes.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.000
Now we can message and call each other.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.610
What should we do next?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.190
Should we study together?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.320
I don't want to study.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.320
It's too annoying.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.490
Should we do something to have fun, then?

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.280
I like simply sitting and talking.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.740
I understand.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.000
What should we talk about, then?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.210
What do you want to talk about?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.920
Nothing in particular.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.130
You're always so honest.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.380
Is being honest a problem?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.510
Generally, you'd call it a virtue.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.720
But it can be problematic at times.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.140
For example?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.270
For example, let me ask you, do you like me?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.350
No. I wouldn't say I do or do not like you.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.980
That's very honest.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.740
Such words could hurt a person
depending on the circumstances.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:07.160
Though I prefer that honesty,
and not having to guess at people's feelings.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.870
Everything should be that simple.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.710
I guess we can talk about something trivial.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.670
Something meaningless that would make us sleepy,

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.920
just a comfortable conversation.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.170
For example?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.720
Let's see...

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.140
We can try searching for
the kindest words in this world.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.640
The kindest words?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.810
It could be fun words or happy words.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.610
It could be anything,
but I chose kind words this time.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.900
What are the kindest words to you?

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.660
I don't know.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.120
Let's think more specifically, then.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:06:00.330
Let's say there's a starving cat sleeping
on chilling asphalt on a cold night,

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.380
very exhausted, and in need of food...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.130
Are there any words that could save it?

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:12.510
<i>I'm sure that cat would be suffering.</i>

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.520
<i>What it would need wouldn't be words.</i>

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.520
<i>It could be saved with some milk and a blanket.</i>

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.520
<i>Would it even be possible to save it with just words?</i>

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.860
You don't need to think about it so seriously.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.910
There's no answer to a meaningless question.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.490
Just say whatever comes to mind.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.870
Then, I'd say, "I'll bring you what you need".

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.380
For example, I'd promise that
I'd bring milk and a blanket to that cat.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.210
I see.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.590
A promise would give it hope.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.090
Hope?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:49.300
If there's help coming to it,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:54.060
the cat might try to endure
a bit more cold and hunger.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.310
What both people and cats
need to endure pain is hope.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.520
Is hope a kind word?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.810
I'm not sure.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.480
Maybe it's just cruel.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:10.400
Maybe the next day, the cat would
be freezing and hungry again.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.030
But I think the feeling that you
want to give someone hope

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.790
is definitely kind.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.500
I see.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.670
What are the kindest words to you?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:29.720
Well, if there were a cat suffering
from hunger and trembling from cold,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.720
I'd say, "isn't it cold?".

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.180
I'd say, "it's cold, and I'm hungry".

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.510
Would that save the cat?

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.140
Of course not.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:41.140
No matter what I'd say, nothing would change.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:45.820
But at the very least,
I'd be able to convey to it that I feel the same.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.070
And what comes from conveying that?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.030
Depends on what it does.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.530
If the cat said it'd try to find food,
I'd answer, "okay, let's go".

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:58.580
If it said that it wanted a warm place to sleep,
I'd go search for one with it.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.040
What if the cat said nothing?

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.290
I'd also say nothing, and just sleep next to it.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.670
<i>What would Kei do?</i>

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.140
I believe that's a sincere answer.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.730
What do you mean?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:24.810
You accept the reality the way it is.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.190
Is that kind?

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.480
I wouldn't know.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:34.200
But I believe the cat would be saved in some way.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.280
I see. I'm glad.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:38.370
Me too.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.330
But you know,

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.420
I don't really trust what we call "words".

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.880
You can't trust words?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.960
If I put what I'm thinking into words,

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.130
it makes me feel like my words belong to someone else.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.380
It's a bit unpleasant.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:09:00.140
For example, when I'm petting
a cat, it's a sign of love.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.270
But how could I show that
amount of love using words?

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.020
I don't know.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.570
I'm sorry.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.360
I said something stupid.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.280
No.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.780
But that's exactly why I wanted
some trivial conversation.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:25.410
There's no right answer, and no one will be troubled
if we don't manage to convey our meaning clearly.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.170
I like this kind of simple, comfortable conversation.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.840
I see.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.420
Please tell me, then.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.420
What?

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.720
How to hold trivial conversations that
would have no meaning and make you sleepy.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.180
Simple, comfortable conversations.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.600
What we just talked about
was exactly a trivial conversation.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.770
Don't worry. You can do it just fine.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.990
<i>And then we talked about
everything that came to mind.</i>

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.030
<i>About a dream I had recently.</i>

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.160
<i>About the shapes of clouds.</i>

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.120
<i>About the cats' paws.</i>

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.790
<i>None of it had any meaning.</i>

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.160
<i>They were conversations for their own sake,</i>

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.580
<i>that we would forget the next day.</i>

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.180
Have we managed to become friends?

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:22.050
I wonder.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:26.020
Rather than friends,
we're still more like acquaintances.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.810
I see...

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.270
Come here the next time you feel like it.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.570
Will it make us friends?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.820
I think that when you talk just once,
you're acquaintances,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.950
but when you talk a lot, you're friends.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.110
Is that how it works?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.580
I don't really know, but I think so.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.080
And I quite like you, actually.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.750
We'll become friends eventually.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.420
I was actually worried.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:55.670
Until now, there was only
one person I could call a friend.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:56.880
One?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.340
Do you mean Asai?

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.380
No, someone else.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.640
I see.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.650
Yes.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.860
I feel like Kei isn't in the "friends" category.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.950
Next time, I'll bring cream puffs from Sangatsudou.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.530
Okay, I'll be waiting.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.700
Yes.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.720
<i>And so, my plan to make a friend began.</i>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.520
<i>Though I don't know yet when I'll see the results of it.</i>

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.520
<i>Asai Kei caught a cold and didn't come to school.</i>

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.270
<i>It wasn't really unusual for him not to feel well.</i>

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.150
<i>It happens a few times a year.</i>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.400
<i>There are three problems, though.</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.740
<i>First, should I go visit him?</i>

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:48.160
<i>Second, if I do, what should I bring?</i>

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.750
<i>And third, should I help U-Research or not?</i>

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.210
Hello!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.590
Can I eat with you?

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.300
You look kind of languid today.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.760
What does that mean?

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:14.640
You know, just, Asai caught a cold and isn't
here today, so I figured you'd be languid.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.230
I see.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.820
You're going to visit him, right?

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:20.900
I'm considering it.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.110
Why?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.610
You should go!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.530
Do you think it's the right thing to do?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.860
Of course!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.990
You can't waste such a great love event!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.620
There's no connection between love and colds.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.830
There is!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.540
You should aim for him exactly
when he's sick and weak!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.790
Misora, you know what's the quickest
and simplest way to cure a cold?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.590
Taking medicine and sleeping a lot?

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.920
I'm not talking about realistic methods here,

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.010
more, you know, miracle-of-love methods!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.890
First, when you kiss someone,
you catch the cold from them.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:53.220
Second, when you give
someone your cold, it's cured.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.640
And that means kissing cures colds!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:57.980
So logical!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.810
That's impossible.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.360
The logic there isn't wrong,

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.980
but the basic premises are.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.610
It's one of the things U-Research is researching.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.870
"Are colds really cured when
someone catches them from you?"

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.200
What's U-Research?

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.490
It's exactly what the name suggests.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.950
The "U" comes from "unidentified".

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:20.330
Basically, in U-Research we research
anything that is unidentified.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:25.550
Let's say I catch a cold
from Kei and his cold is cured.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:30.760
I don't think it can be proven just from that
situation that giving someone a cold cures it.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.850
It could've just been cured afterwards.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.970
That's why you check if the
cold was given to someone

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.440
between catching a cold and its curing

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.100
and look at statistics, that's the point!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.270
I think infecting people with your cold

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.610
usually just happens without you noticing.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:46.990
Yeah.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.360
It's probably impossible to gather proper statistics.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.120
Isn't it then pointless?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.120
Exactly!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.700
The true purpose of U-Research
is researching pointless things

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.460
and deciding on the results by ourselves!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.460
I see.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:04.920
So if you feel like it, try kissing Asai.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.800
<i>I was asked by Minami Mirai to help her research.</i>

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:15.180
<i>I would if there weren't any problems,</i>

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.810
<i>but Asai Kei is involved in this case.</i>

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:22.150
<i>Kei probably wouldn't want to give anyone his cold.</i>

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:26.190
<i>And that means I can't help U-Research with this.</i>

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:31.240
<i>What's more important, his stomach
might be weak because of the cold,</i>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:36.950
<i>and I heard that a warm meal,
easily digestable and rich in carbohydrates,</i>

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.160
<i>increases body temperature
and immune response.</i>

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:43.830
<i>So I'll go with a well-known
comfort food: rice porridge.</i>

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.260
<i>Dried kelp, check.</i>

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.390
<i>Rice, check.</i>

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.140
<i>Pot, check.</i>

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:04.770
<i>Kei should have salt and other spices
in his house, so I'll just borrow them.</i>

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.820
<i>It's difficult to walk.</i>

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.490
<i>I always feel like this when I'm alone.</i>

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:20.500
<i>When Kei isn't next to me,
I feel like my balance is disrupted.</i>

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:24.370
<i>I wonder if my heavy bag is making it worse.</i>

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.170
<i>I know!</i>

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.590
<i>If I carry it on the side Kei walks on,</i>

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.840
<i>it might help with the balance a bit.</i>

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.970
<i>Nothing really changed.</i>

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.720
<i>There's nothing I can do. I should just hurry.</i>

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.560
<i>I should have everything necessary.</i>

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.810
<i>No, let's check it again.</i>

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.480
<i>Once I get to Kei's,
it'll be too late to go back for anything.</i>

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.360
<i>First, rice.</i>

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.570
<i>Dried kelp.</i>

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.740
<i>A pot.</i>

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.200
<i>I'll be borrowing spices, so I'm missing...</i>

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.870
<i>I know! Dried plums!</i>

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.040
<i>Dried plums are a staple of rice porridge.</i>

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:04.870
<i>I don't know the details, but I heard they're healthy.</i>

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.000
<i>I'm glad I rechecked everything.</i>

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.090
<i>I'll buy them on the way there.</i>

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:20.510
<i>Seems like the balance is still the same,
despite adding the plums.</i>

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.520
<i>Sangatsudou...</i>

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.780
<i>They have sweets in there.</i>

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.530
<i>Kei likes sweet things.</i>

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:36.910
<i>Still, I don't think it's appropriate
for a sick person to eat sweets.</i>

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.280
<i>Peaches! Right, peaches!</i>

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.700
<i>Peaches are an obvious choice.</i>

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:45.000
<i>I don't know where I heard it, but I feel like
something like this was commonly known.</i>

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.090
Welcome!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.340
Two Peach Jellies please.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.970
I'm terribly sorry, but we've sold out already today.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.100
How about this Fruit Tart instead?

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.970
It's filled with peaches, too.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.890
<i>I'm sure Kei likes tarts.</i>

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.980
<i>But would he want to eat one when he has a cold?</i>

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.350
<i>I know!</i>

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:20.950
<i>That's a problem.</i>

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:26.250
<i>I don't know what to do
if I can't get advice from a specialist.</i>

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.040
What will you do?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.250
<i>Right! I have a specialist right here too!</i>

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.340
<i>Someone working at Sangatsudou.</i>

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.630
<i>Who else would be a better person to ask?</i>

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.970
Do you have something good for eating when you're sick?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.300
Are you visiting someone?

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.390
Yes.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.720
How about ice cream?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.480
<i>Ice cream...</i>

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:52.690
<i>It does seem to be nice to eat
something cold when you have a fever.</i>

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.570
<i>But that's not peaches.</i>

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.690
Ice cream is great when you're sick.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.860
Better than peaches?

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:02.740
Peaches are good, but ice cream is better.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.620
Even though that's not peaches?

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.620
We don't have peach ice cream,

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.660
but I recommend apple ice cream.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.710
<i>Apple...</i>

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.590
<i>Apples might be nice for visiting someone.</i>

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.000
<i>I feel like they are.</i>

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:17.800
Fruit Tart

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.380
<i>Peaches, but in a tart...
Fruit Tart</i>

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.430
<i>Not peaches, but ice cream.</i>

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:24.140
<i>And they have apple!</i>

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:30.480
Two tubs of apple ice cream, then.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.230
Sure, just a moment.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.320
<i>The weight of the plums got
counterbalanced by the ice cream.</i>

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.490
<i>The balance is so bad I can't walk.</i>

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:43.950
<i>But now it's perfect.</i>

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:49.200
<i>Rice, dried kelp, a pot, dried plums, apple ice cream.</i>

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.750
<i>I hope Kei will be happy.</i>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:53.920
<i>But...</i>

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:58.920
<i>To visit him, I need to ring the doorbell.</i>

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.380
<i>And he'd have to unlock the door for me.</i>

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>I'd wake him up when he's resting in bed,</i>

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.060
<i>and make him walk to the door.</i>

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.600
<i>Is it worth it just for rice porridge and ice cream?</i>

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:15.730
<i>Maybe he already prepared dinner for himself.</i>

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:20.030
<i>I've never visited him before.</i>

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:25.120
<i>Asai Kei is excellent at everything,
so he can handle most things by himself.</i>

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:27.990
<i>It's not a problem for him that he's alone.</i>

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:31.750
<i>There's no reason to be worried about him.</i>

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.050
<i>I should go home...</i>

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.560
<i>For some reason, I really want some ice cream.</i>

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.020
<i>If you have time, could you buy some for me?</i>

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.980
<i>Like the specialist said!</i>

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.450
<i>Ice cream is better than peaches after all!</i>

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.400
<i>I should hurry to Kei's—</i>

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.030
<i>This is weird.</i>

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.740
<i>That's not the kind of message Kei would send.</i>

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.000
<i>There's no way he'd use people
to do something for him.</i>

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.920
Minami, right?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:22.880
Hi.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.090
Were you following me the whole time?

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.720
Well, how should I put it...

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.850
I'm sorry!

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:33.390
Why did you do that?

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.270
I thought it'd be fun...

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.770
Was it fun?

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:38.770
In its own way!

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.980
The best part was how
you passed the confectionery,

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.950
changed your mind, and went back there!

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.610
I don't understand what's fun about it.

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.700
But you failed, Misora.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.240
Why didn't you go to Asai's?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.790
Because I realized there's no need to.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.580
I don't think you need a reason to visit a sick friend.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:01.960
I realized I actually could bother him if I went.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:04.090
So I should just give up.

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:06.590
You wouldn't! He'd be happy!

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:08.550
Kei is the one to decide that.

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.100
That's not true!

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.060
Anyone would be happy, I'm sure!

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:15.730
And that's why you contacted Kei, right?

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:18.730
Yeah, I thought I couldn't let this chance slip by,

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:20.810
so I told him to contact you...

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:22.650
I see.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:23.360
Yeah.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:26.240
Thank you.

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:29.950
No problem.

00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:35.450
I'll go eat ice cream with Kei, then.

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:36.620
You should.

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:38.460
Try feeding him.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:40.000
I will.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:41.960
What?! You really will?

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:45.590
Isn't that what you do when you visit a sick person?

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:50.090
Yeah, I think...

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:52.550
I think that's just how visits should go.

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.100
Well, good luck then!

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:56.180
Thank you.

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:13.370
So if you feel like it, try kissing Asai.

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:18.870
<b>Apple</b>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.500
Next Episode

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.380
Welcome! To the world of dreams!

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:29.260
There's someone I want to meet.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.090
I want to be like a god.
There's someone I want to meet.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:31.010
I want to be like a god.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:31.720
It's inverted...
I want to be like a god.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:32.050
It's inverted...

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:32.510
Michiru is still Michiru.
It's inverted...

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.760
Michiru is still Michiru.

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:34.430
I'm supposed to destroy this world.
Michiru is still Michiru.

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.810
I'm supposed to destroy this world.

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:37.270
Please wait!
I'm supposed to destroy this world.

00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:37.770
Please wait!

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:47.780
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:55.280
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:55.870 --> 00:24:00.750
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:08.800
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:14.390
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:21.560
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:26.110
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:29.440
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:35.450
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:42.580
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:42.580 --> 00:24:49.090
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:49.090 --> 00:24:56.260
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:56.260 --> 00:25:00.350
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:00.350 --> 00:25:07.190
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
